{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books","id":7865,"title":"Who likes books, I like books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-10T21:43:00-08:00","id":7865,"title":"Who likes books, I like books","content":"what kind of books do you guys like? I've always been a fan of fantasy. I like the Tolkien level of fantasy so some magic, some other races but most of the time wizards aren't riding dragons and casting bolts of chaos energy out of their staffs and shit like that. Somewhat recently, last 2 or 3 years, I've really taken an interest in biographies. Well written ones. I can't stand the dry info dump bullet point biographies. I'm going to be borrowing one from the library soon by Edmund Morris about Beethoven. After that one I found one for William McKinley I want to read because some of the least known presidents were some of the most badass. Just having done some research on McKinley I found out he served in the Civil War, was the president during the post Civil War depression, pulled us out of it and after being elected for his second term with Theodore Roosevelt as his Vice President was shot and died 8 days later. Most people don't even know we had a 3rd president get assassinated much less who he was and I want to find out that information. <br /> <br /> On the much less real and much more fictional end of books, I am going to actually finally start reading Game of Thrones and that stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:03:54-08:00","id":7947,"title":"","content":"I tend to like fiction the most, specially Fantasy and Horror. Currently I'm reading both the last (5th) book of a Song of Ice and Fire and also started reading the Necroscope series (already read the first 2 books, 3 to go).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:18:56-08:00","id":7954,"title":"","content":"I love urban fantasy. Specially the Dresden Files series. I tend to go with science fiction or sword and sorcery but normally something that catches my eye. I have the Disneys John Carter books (i buy one everytime i go to the USA). I have the entire Dragonlance series of Raistlin from soulforge until the end. The drizzts books and the game of thrones series.<br /> <br /> I read the Finder as i love the short lived TV series. Currently im re reading Cold Days of the Dresden FIles as most of my reading time is spent reading all the Ascension books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T04:34:28-08:00","id":7974,"title":"","content":"Generally there's some degree of fantasy or sci-fi in things I like, but beyond that there really are no hard-and-fast rules about the genre. What I'm more drawn in by is the style of a work--things that try and bend the standard story arc of their genre, to either a darker or more complex plot--<i>A Song of Ice and Fire, </i>most notably, but also things like <i>The Brotherband Chronicles</i> that feature as their main characters Viking-equivalents who aren't consistently smashing things to solve problems, and criminals who aren't the purely amoral and lawbreaking stereotype, or the noble thief stereotype, and actually the first three <i>Maximum Ride</i> books, which even though they don't seem like they do that actually do go into what it means to be a warped science experiment with certain of the characters, which isn't as often done. I'm also really drawn to the darker end of war novels for whatever reason--<i>The Red Badge of Courage</i>, technically <i>Slaughterhouse 5,</i> etc. <br /> <br /> As for what I'm currently reading--actually something for school, but I really like it: <i>Sabriya, Damascus Bittersweet</i>, about the life of a Syrian girl's aunt before she killed herself, and how it sort of led up to that conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":781,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","user":"Chained Divinity","date":". 11-11-2013, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:03:02-08:00","id":8031,"title":"","content":"Right now I'm reading Rubicon by Steven Saylor, I love ancient Rome. I loved Anita Blake until it became porn, and Sookie Stackhouse before it became stupid (sorry that ending really put me off). I just finished Dracula, the Un-Dead, a sequel by one of Stoker's descendents and it was really good. Glad to see a book post along with the movie one, I read more than I watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:50:18-08:00","id":8162,"title":"","content":"Depends on what I am ordering on eBay. I just ordered &quot;Orphan Train&quot;, a fictional work about the actual Orphan Trains that came out of New York City, taking children out west to be adopt. Some were put in good homes, some were used for slave labor.<br /> <br /> I also got horror, sci-fi, romance, biblical fiction, various occult (yes, if I want, I can make charms and they work unless someone steals them.) I have been studying shamanism to be closer to my NA side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:16:03-08:00","id":8185,"title":"","content":"I love books.<br /> <br /> Right now, I am on Book Ten of the Wheel of Time series by Robert Jordan and Brandon Sanderson.<br /> <br /> Do any of you use Goodreads? I find it is a great tool for tracking what I have read, sharing with others, and learning about new reading opportunities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:38:15-08:00","id":8211,"title":"","content":"I am a book addict and used to work for Barnes &amp; Noble in a &quot;junkie/dealer&quot; situation (sold books to pay for my own books). Currently, I'm plodding my way thru <a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/book/show/55236.The_Irony_of_American_History\" target=\"_blank\">The Irony of American History by Reinhold Niebuhr</a>, <a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/book/show/9533378-hounded?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\">Hounded by Kevin Hearne</a>, and rereading <a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/search?utf8=%E2%9C%93&amp;query=the+dresden+files\" target=\"_blank\">The Dresden Files</a> again from the beginning, I was just about to start on <a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/book/show/17683.Dead_Beat?from_search=true\" target=\"_blank\">Dead Beat</a> when my job put a halt to my ability to use audiobooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:07:16-08:00","id":8315,"title":"","content":"I like nonfiction, fiction books don't usually have that &quot;choose your own adventure&quot; feel I like from RPGs.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm reading...<br /> <br /> Gravity and Grace by Simone Weil<br /> <br /> Genesis and Apocalypse: A Theological Voyage Towards Authentic Christianity by Thomas Altizer<br /> <br /> The Cost of Discipleship by Dietrich Bonhoeffer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T06:20:32-08:00","id":8753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=7954#post7954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love urban fantasy. Specially the Dresden Files series. I tend to go with science fiction or sword and sorcery but normally something that catches my eye. I have the Disneys John Carter books (i buy one everytime i go to the USA). I have the entire Dragonlance series of Raistlin from soulforge until the end. The drizzts books and the game of thrones series.<br /> <br /> I read the Finder as i love the short lived TV series. Currently im re reading Cold Days of the Dresden FIles as most of my reading time is spent reading all the Ascension books.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Father just had a heart attack, he does everytime someone says &quot;Disney's John Carter&quot;. John Carter, Tarzan, and Carson of Venus as well as Pellucidar are all written by Edgar Rice Burroughs. Who as my Father will tell you is the greatest author to ever live...<br /> <br /> Yes I have at one point or another actually read all of those series. I generally read horror, fantasy, and sci-fi. I am not a big fan of Dean Koontz=. I like Stephan King but I have to be in the mood to read him. My favorite horror author is Robert R McCammon, I think Mystery Walk is one of the best coming of age stories ever written and it has demons and ghosts! I am also addicted to Nora Roberts and her works particularly the In Death series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":".  corrected my fat finger typos. 11-12-2013, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:08:29-08:00","id":8822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=8753#post8753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My Father just had a heart attack, he does everytime someone says &quot;Disney's John Carter&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the Disney movie and it got me reading john carter however i was talking about a version that disney sells. <br /> <br /> This one:<br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-GdN0wgYnmuI/T2DEkZ-fGLI/AAAAAAAAESM/4eb06XJ4U64/s1600/tumblr_m0fitfM2wR1qh991go1_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It has some lovely details on the pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:34:12-08:00","id":8878,"title":"","content":"That looks like an update on some of the old serial work I've seen I'll have to look for this when I get up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:47:17-08:00","id":12368,"title":"","content":"I liked fantasy a lot more when I was younger. I suppose Glen Cook and Tanith Lee are my favorites, but I don't like a lot of stuff that comes out now in fantasy. Some authors I do like now are Aliette de Bodard, who writes a fantasy/alternate history version of Aztec society before the fall, starring a priest of death, KJ Parker, who does great characters in their own low fantasy world. I've recently enjoyed James Enge and AE Marling.<br /> <br /> About ten years or so ago I got into reading horror. It's a lot like fantasy, most of the popular stuff is wildly similar or run by big names, but I've found a few recent gems in Charlee Jacob (who practically writes within the world of darkness) and Laird Barron, who has a lot of fantastically dark ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:59:04-08:00","id":49452,"title":"","content":"Today I finally received <i>Harrius Potter et Philosophi Lapis</i>. I've been waiting two weeks and therefore am giddy. <br /> <br /> &lt;------ See that? That's me giddy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T19:09:44-08:00","id":49461,"title":"","content":"Getting more Anne McCaffrey books in, reading Dinosaur Planet right now. Need to organize the shelves in my bedroom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T02:51:47-08:00","id":49656,"title":"","content":"I'm currently rereading The Great and Secret Show by Clive Barker. I'm enjoying it like it's the first time I'm reading it. The Jaffe is a sad, interesting figure. Really, the book's full of characters I'd love to sit down with, simply to &quot;pick their brains&quot; about things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T04:58:05-08:00","id":49695,"title":"","content":"Right now I am reading Sisterhood of Dune, then I will read Johnny Alucard. And yeah, The Great &amp; Secret Show is amazing, and it's sequel (Everville I think?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T05:20:33-08:00","id":49703,"title":"","content":"My sister got me a copy of <b>Hyperbole and a Half</b> for Christmas. I have been limiting my exposure to it because I'm pretty sure it's possible to overdose on laughter, and this book is <i>so fucking funny</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T06:07:09-08:00","id":49731,"title":"","content":"Currently reading The Bully Pulpit by Dorris Kearns Goodwin. The book is good, the information is good, the formating is good, the editing... leaves a lot to be desired. It makes it really hard to read the book when there are lots of direct quotes in it and they don't end properly but after the &quot;bla bla bla bla bloo bloo bloo said Fignarfus Korinton&quot; the quote is obviously supposed to be after the last bloo not where they let it. sloppy editing is ruining my enjoyment of this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T06:30:31-08:00","id":49741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=49703#post49703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My sister got me a copy of <b>Hyperbole and a Half</b> for Christmas. I have been limiting my exposure to it because I'm pretty sure it's possible to overdose on laughter, and this book is <i>so fucking funny</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first book I've read in a long time that I kept putting down because I didn't want it to end.<br /> <br /> I'm currently reading <i>Lies My Teacher Told Me</i> and working my way through the <i>Culture</i> series by Iain M. Banks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T07:07:26-08:00","id":50651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=8185#post8185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of you use Goodreads?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do...<br /> <br /> I'm going through the Dexter series since my supervisor can't help but throw them books at mah face...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/170-lunatyk","name":"Lunatyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T07:48:47-08:00","id":50684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People who give other people that book are good people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your point of view. One of the main gifts I was handing out this year were copies of Baby's First Mythos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:01:58-08:00","id":50795,"title":"","content":"Started Dinosaur Planet Survivors last night. Had my niece sleeping with me so I got tired quick. She kept kneeing my butt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T12:18:24-08:00","id":50931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=50684#post50684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on your point of view. One of the main gifts I was handing out this year were copies of Baby's First Mythos</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a store where they have the Cthulhu plushy dolls, I've been so tempted to get one for my Baby Bears. My two little loonies play at scaring each other as the monster, like to watch Monsters Inc, Criminal Minds, Supernatural and Grimm with us, and were into Halloween more for the &quot;boos&quot; (the decorations) than the candy. I think they are the type of kids who that plushy was made for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-16-2014, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T15:02:57-08:00","id":51090,"title":"","content":"Send me one...I fear I don't have enough yarn to make myself another Cthulhu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T15:32:05-08:00","id":51108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=8185#post8185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love books.<br /> <br /> Right now, I am on Book Ten of the Wheel of Time series by Robert Jordan and Brandon Sanderson.<br /> <br /> Do any of you use Goodreads? I find it is a great tool for tracking what I have read, sharing with others, and learning about new reading opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am into the parts written by Brandon Sanderson now, and WOW! Brandon is a phenomenal writer. I love his style, and he took a series I was already enjoying, and made it even better. I am going to check out some of his other books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T15:56:53-08:00","id":51125,"title":"","content":"I have to stick to Mom when we go to the library...I know who the authors are and she is not into horror and paranormal. She liked The Stand and Bag of Bones when they was broadcasted (that is the only way she will stand King). She used to read Hillerman but now she doesn't. Romance, mystery, medical thrillers (she read all of Robin Cook). I like historical fiction, read all of the Sookie Stackhouse books (saving money for season 6), sci-fi. She does not know about the roleplaying books I got stashed away. Used to read medical textbooks but lost them in the fire years ago.<br /> <br /> I probably order her another lot next month and start selling the ones she don't want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T17:15:13-08:00","id":51198,"title":"","content":"I love books. I have a Nook and have far too many books. I'm currently re-reading Dresden Files from the beginning. The book I'm most into right now is S by JJ Abrams and Doug Dorst. It is absolutely fantastic, and should only be read as a real book, not a digital copy. It has all sorts of props and stuff to go along with the three story lines. It even came with a decoder wheel that I still don't know what to do with. Anyone who likes books should read S. I also have the Sword of Shannara going for the first time. It's not too bad. I generally like sci fi, fantasy, urban fantasy and historical non fiction. Yay books lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T19:11:08-08:00","id":52072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=49656#post49656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently rereading The Great and Secret Show by Clive Barker. I'm enjoying it like it's the first time I'm reading it. The Jaffe is a sad, interesting figure. Really, the book's full of characters I'd love to sit down with, simply to &quot;pick their brains&quot; about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely book! Everville and Galilee are &quot;kinda, sorta&quot; sequels, IIRC. If you haven't read Weaveworld and Imacija, then I can't recommend them enough!<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm switching back and forth between The Blinding Knife by Brian Weeks, The Republic of Thieves by Scott Lynch, and Brandon Sanderson's Mistborn. When those wear me out, I'm rereading The Stars My Destination by Alfred Bester...<br /> <br /> So, yeah, my fiction tastes are mostly Fantasy/SF, with a bit of Horror thrown in (Thomas Ligotti, why have you forsaken us?!); I can't remember the last novel I read with no supernatural elements in it! I also enjoy historical books, esp of the &quot;conspiracy&quot; type!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:00:09-08:00","id":53828,"title":"","content":"atm I'm reading Light Fantastic by Terry Pratchett, the second book from the Discworld series. It's FANTASTIC. For anyone that is a adventure/fantasy lover this IS A MUST TO READ. <br /> <br /> Abit about the first main character from the wiki:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rincewind\" target=\"_blank\">Rincewind</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> was the first protagonist of </span></span><i>Discworld</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">; a wizard with no skill, no wizardly qualifications and no interest in heroics. He is the archetypal coward, but is constantly thrust into extremely dangerous adventures. In </span></span><i>The Last Hero</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, he flatly states that he does </span></span><i>not</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> wish to join an expedition to explore over the edge of the Disc\u2014but, being fully geared for the expedition at the time, clarifies by saying that any amount of protesting on his part is futile, as something will eventually occur that will bring him into the expedition anyway. As such, he not only constantly succeeds in staying alive, but also saves </span></span><i>Discworld</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> on several occasions,</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1014-oh-goth","name":"Oh Goth...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:53:37-08:00","id":54085,"title":"","content":"For people not familiar with Discworld, it's a decidedly humorous fantasy setting, which stands to reason since it started out as a piss-take on many of the typical fantasy tropes. It is very very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:33:47-08:00","id":54114,"title":"","content":"I am reading a book called <b>Up Country</b> by someone whose name I forget (I keep trying to call him Cecil B. DeMille, which is clearly wrong). I'm only a hundred or so pages in and really have nothing to say about it, but I can't help observing that I really like books because this was written around 1995 and I can still have a meaningful discussion about it. Try doing that with a movie that came out in 1995.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:03:05-08:00","id":54127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=54114#post54114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am reading a book called <b>Up Country</b> by someone whose name I forget (I keep trying to call him Cecil B. DeMille, which is clearly wrong). I'm only a hundred or so pages in and really have nothing to say about it, but I can't help observing that I really like books because this was written around 1995 and I can still have a meaningful discussion about it. Try doing that with a movie that came out in 1995.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that author (Nelson DeMille) being on the best seller list repeatedly for quite some time.<br /> <br /> He's one of those guys I call a &quot;stealth celebrity author&quot; because he's not a name most people recognize, unless you're into books. But <i>every time</i> he releases a new book, it's on the New York Time Bestseller list for a few weeks and he's got 20+ books to his name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-20-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:58:34-08:00","id":54220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oh Goth...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=53828#post53828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">atm I'm reading Light Fantastic by Terry Pratchett, the second book from the Discworld series. It's FANTASTIC. For anyone that is a adventure/fantasy lover this IS A MUST TO READ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rincewind is generally looked upon as the <i>least</i> interesting main character in the Discworld series. It gets even better later on, though there are some duds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:42:22-08:00","id":54968,"title":"","content":"I love stories in any form but the written word has always been my favorite medium. I recently ditched my bookcases because I realized that they actually took up space I could use for more books... So now I have huge stacks of books just lining the walls, on the stairs and to make impromptu tables, chairs and footstools (it sounds terrible, but books are surprisingly durable!). I used to be a librarian and have also worked in bookstores. Now I'm the 'head' of a book-club which really isn't as lame as it sounds (we just did Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream and are now reading Roald Dahl's Sometime Never: A Fable for Supermen. Its a very eclectic group and the books we read reflect that). I also write my own stories but I just don't seem to find that special something that makes me feel like they're actually good. I think I have good ideas but don't execute them very well...<br /> There's no genre I dislike, though there are plenty of authors I think that don't deserve to have their work published (I'm an elitist that way). Most of the books I read are classics, if only because I want to know what makes them classic and because they rarely disappoint. I've recently discovered Haruki Murakami's What I Talk About When I Talk About Running (I'm a runner too, so...) and have since voraciously read most of his fiction work. I'm looking forward to his next work as I thought IQ84 was relatively weak compared to his other works. I'm currently rereading The Wind-Up Bird Chronicle for myself while reading Sometime Never: A Fable for Supermen for the bookclub. Next up is probably The Sirens of Titan by Kurt Vonnegut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T07:19:15-07:00","id":123130,"title":"","content":"Recently, I've been reading for fun. (Huzzah!)<br /> <br /> Things I've read:<br /> <br /> I read the <i>Hunger Games</i> trilogy. The first book was okay. I really liked <i>Catching Fire</i>, loved the ending. I hated <i>Mockingjay</i>.<br /> <br /> I read the <i>Darkest Powers</i> trilogy by Kelley Armstrong. It left some things unresolved (there's a sequel trilogy, which I just started) but I quite enjoyed it. <br /> <br /> I read the first of the <i>League of Extraordinary Gentlemen</i>. It was &quot;meh&quot;. Nothing spectacular in my opinion. <br /> <br /> Yesterday, I finished <i>Percy Jackson and the Sea of Monsters</i>. I liked this one significantly more than the first book. I don't know if it was because of my state of mind going into it, or if it's really better, but whatever the reason, I liked it more. <br /> <br /> As stated, next up is Kelley Armstrong's <i>Darkness Rising</i> trilogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T14:41:31-07:00","id":123423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=51108#post51108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am into the parts written by Brandon Sanderson now, and WOW! Brandon is a phenomenal writer. I love his style, and he took a series I was already enjoying, and made it even better. I am going to check out some of his other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Sanderson is a good writer but unfortunately he couldn't quite pull it off with the last book. Memory of light required him to write in much larger scale than his comfortable with and unfortunately it shows. Having read the whole of WoT more than once i've become convinced that Jordan fell victim to loving his own voice too much which his ailing health wasn't helping and Sanderson did the best he could with what he had thus making the series still good and satisfactory but which had potential for so much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T16:09:55-07:00","id":123471,"title":"","content":"Just finished <i>The Gathering</i>, the first book in the <i>Darkness Rising</i> trilogy. It's enjoyable enough. Could not stand alone. Seems really slow, too. It's a supernatural book, but I'm not sure who's supernatural and what their powers are yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T04:09:43-07:00","id":128862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=123130#post123130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yesterday, I finished <i>Percy Jackson and the Sea of Monsters</i>. I liked this one significantly more than the first book. I don't know if it was because of my state of mind going into it, or if it's really better, but whatever the reason, I liked it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Scion fodder, <a href=\"http://olympiansrule.com/aboutTheGods.html\" target=\"_blank\">George O' Connor</a>'s works might be worth a look too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:28:51-07:00","id":224207,"title":"","content":"So, I'm rereading <i>Jurassic Park</i> after about 15 years. It's not nearly as good as I remember it being. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The writing just seems lacking. Most of the characters seem kind of one dimensional; you don't really get much insight into why they are the people that are. That might be the style of book, though.<br /> <br /> Tim is supposed to be 11, but I feel like he acts more like a 14-15 year old. Lex is supposed to be 8, but acts like she's 6.<br /> <br /> Doctor Grant magically knows that frog DNA will allow the dinosaurs to reproduce while Doctor Wu, the chief geneticist, can't fathom why Grant asked about frog DNA. On the other hand, Doctor Wu is giving pointers to Arnold, the engineer, on debugging the computer system that Nedry sabotaged. (Maybe that's why he can't figure out why the frog DNA is relevant: because he skipped that class and took a programming class instead. :-P )<br /> <br /> Also, the book was published in 1990 and really shows its age with the way it describes the computer systems.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That being said, as is to be expected, the book is a lot more detailed than the movie, and does a lot of things better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T21:05:31-07:00","id":241036,"title":"","content":"Does anyone like Gothic horror? I want to start sampling the genre, but don't know where to start,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T23:38:22-07:00","id":241140,"title":"","content":"I lost the taste for fiction somewhere in the last few years and have been eating a pretty steady diet of history books. I'm currently on The World of the Shining Prince, Court Life in Ancient Japan which presents the Heian period as something almost approaching some kind of cosmic joke. The section on taboo directions and how it made an already ossified nobility even more useless was pretty amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T06:50:46-07:00","id":241300,"title":"","content":"Did the post I made last night get eaten?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T10:48:36-07:00","id":241477,"title":"","content":"I flagged the thread for deletion when I noticed this thread's existence, though that didn't stop the system from notifying me that you'd posted in the thread. What did you say, Jeddy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T15:17:08-07:00","id":241754,"title":"","content":"All right. Well, first off, I posted a link to this thread, which appears to no longer be needed.<br /> <br /> Then, I said, the only gothic horror that I've read is <i>Dracula</i>, which is fantastic. I highly recommend it. It holds up to its reputation.<br /> <br /> I just finished the His Dark Materials trilogy. I really liked it. It was one of the best written books that I've read in a long time. One of the reviews on the dust jacket said something to the effect of, &quot;It's the best fantasy since <i>Lord of the Rings</i>.&quot; It's probably the best fantasy that I've read since I read <i>Lord of the Rings</i> (about a year ago).<br /> <br /> Next up I'm going to finish the <i>Hex Hall</i> series (I've already read the first book, so I'm into the second now). They're not great works of literature, but they're light, and fluffy and fun. A needed diversion for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T15:52:11-07:00","id":241773,"title":"","content":"I've read <b>Dracula</b> a few times, and...not bad, and I actually kind of like the focus on the power of love and all that, but not my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, I still need to look up that series of comic books made of old novels like those. When I was a kid, that one scared the piss out of me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: See, it turns out I define &quot;Gothic horror&quot; by different standards than, well, than academia does. I think of it as an oppressive horror in which protagonists are bound by chains of obligations to remain in proximity to dangerous situations with cruel, unfair rules the characters don't understand and can't follow but are punished for breaking. That is not exactly what it is. Hell, I've probably done a better job of defining dark fairy tales than Gothic horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 08-26-2014, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T07:43:18-07:00","id":242242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/7865-who-likes-books-i-like-books?p=241773#post241773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: See, it turns out I define &quot;Gothic horror&quot; by different standards than, well, than academia does. I think of it as an oppressive horror in which protagonists are bound by chains of obligations to remain in proximity to dangerous situations with cruel, unfair rules the characters don't understand and can't follow but are punished for breaking. That is not exactly what it is. Hell, I've probably done a better job of defining dark fairy tales than Gothic horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've gotten kind of specific, but there's nothing there that couldn't be used in a Gothic horror story.<br /> <br /> I mean, if we break down <b>Dracula </b>a bit, we see how the protagonists are caught up in the story thru no choice of their own and by chains of coincidence <b>too </b>specific to be properly dismissed as <i>coincidence</i>. They don't properly understand why Dracula is interested in Mina, and without Van Helsing's help, they never would have understood the rules for dealing with vampires in general and Dracula in particular, and Lucy <i>certainly </i>paid the price for their lack of knowledge. As far as not being able to escape the situation due to proximity, Dracula started out nearly a continent away (check a map for Romania to England, per Google maps, 2,490.1 km) and still got his teeth into Lucy and Mina. There <i>wasn't</i> a place far enough away.<br /> <br /> Really, Gothic fiction just needs a few elements of the ancient, barbaric times (hence the title &quot;gothic&quot;) coming back to disrupt the orderly, modern world, some kind of mystery about the who's and why's that must be solved before it will all go away, and a really good chance that not everybody is going to make it out alive/sane/whole. After that, well, just look at some of the stories that are considered to be &quot;gothic&quot;. THE NUTCRACKER started out as a short story written by one of the top German Gothic fiction authors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T09:40:00-07:00","id":242292,"title":"","content":"If I recall, the original Nutcracker story doesn't exactly have a happy ending.<br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> I tend to look at the Cthulhu mythos stuff for gothic horror, where the longer the story, the less sane the protagonists seem to be by the end. And that's assuming any are alive by then.<br /> <br /> &quot;Arkham Horror&quot; is a recent publisher of Cthulhu related stuff, (produced however by Fantasy flight Games). I've not read any of them however.<br /> <br /> Hmm...and perhaps these gems might be of interest;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Arcanum-Thomas-Wheeler/dp/0553381997\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Thomas_Wheeler_-_The_Arcanum.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The year is 1919 and Sir Arthur Conan Doyle must investigate the murder of his mentor (and founder of the The Arcanum), Konstantin Duvall. To do so he must reunite the scattered members of the Arcanum: Harry Houdini, H. P. Lovecraft, and voodoo queen Marie Laveau. Doyle finds himself embroiled in a story of war as old as time itself, for possession of the world\u2019s most powerful\u2014now missing\u2014artifact: the Book of Enoch, the chronicle of God\u2019s mistakes, within whose pages lie the seeds for the end of everything. Peopled with the twentieth century\u2019s most famous\u2014and infamous\u2014figures, the stakes go beyond the realm of humankind\u2014into the divine.</span></i><br /> <br /> And this one was first published in the mid 70s...an oldie but a goodie, though somewhat formulaic today;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Magicians-James-Gunn/dp/1604599138\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://thumbs1.ebaystatic.com/d/l225/m/mrNI-UaS_45BfbtoOzh7r0w.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <i> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Struggling PI Casey thinks he's finally found an easy score: an elderly woman has just walked into his office and offered him a thousand dollars to find out the real name of a man who calls himself Solomon. Solomon is a magician. Not only does he carry false identification, but he can change his physical appearance at will. One of Solomon's identities is nationally prominent, but another is a power-hungry crook with political ambitions. Casey finds himself at a magicians' convention where no one is who he appears to be and all the tricks seem to lead to death... Casey's death. Casey is caught in the middle of a power struggle between Solomon and Ariel, a young woman out to avenge the death of her father. It's a struggle between black and white magic, and when Casey throws his weight to the good, he may learn a few tricks of his own...</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}